// gen-working.axreg — project-local registry for axAI-axlang-gen-working.
//
// Identities: §5b bootstrap rule — SHA-256 of the UTF-8 function name bytes.
// This is the same rule used by axis-bridge.axreg. Entropy-minted identities
// via registry_compound_id are the long-term goal; §5b is the bootstrap.
//
// Scope: every user-defined function in lib/core/*.ai2, every transition
// compiled from src/ and installed to lib/transitions/, and any generated
// lib functions produced at build time.
//
// TYPE GAPS (no type in the 0.5 vocabulary):
//   int_div_checked — returns Option(Int); no Option type exists yet.
//                     Typed as Value until Option is added to the type system.
//   ir_build_arg_list — takes a heterogeneous list [Int, Value, Value].
//                       Typed as Value in/out until a typed list is available.
//   ir_make_term_from_type_and_str — takes [Int, Text] as a list, returns
//                       a Core IR term. Typed as Value in/out.
// These three require bridge-level type system extension to type correctly.

registry gen-working 0.5

// Unit/Int/Text/Bool/Value/TextList are declared in axis-bridge.axreg,
// co-fed with this registry by every invocation that feeds gen-working.axreg.

// ─────────── lib/core: string utilities ───────────

// str_before: returns substring before first occurrence of needle in s.
// Returns s unchanged if needle not found.

// str_after: returns substring after first occurrence of needle in s.
// Returns s unchanged if needle not found.

// str_between: returns substring between open_delim and close_delim.
// Returns empty string if either delimiter is absent.

// find_from: index of first occurrence of `word` in `buf` at or after position
// `start`. M1-authored composite — body shipped as registries/bodies/find_from.coreir
// with Param-typed pool entries that the bridge substitutes with caller args
// at codegen.
//   identity = sha256("find_from")           (§5b name rule)
//   body     = bundle internal identity      (compiler-emitted at compile time)
fn find_from
  identity 0xa515b4276ab85e44273e190417e86c8535e0d01b45ada32d24e3bdb121e25396
  kind composite
  in (Text, Text, Int)
  out Int
  body 0xd97ed17daf38a6a662965f300bed221a7ced57d5d291f95e6ef9687a94dd9df9
end

// ─────────── lib/core: integer utilities ───────────

// int_min: minimum of two integers.

// int_max: maximum of two integers.

// int_clamp: clamp value to [lo, hi].

// int_div_checked: safe division returning Option(Int).
// TYPE GAP: returns Option(Int) — typed as Value until Option is in vocabulary.

// is_positive: returns 1 if n > 0, else 0.

// ─────────── lib/core: IR utilities ───────────

// ir_make_var_from_int: converts Int to a Core IR Var by wrapping int_to_str + ir_make_var.
// Generated by gen_lib_fn at build time; no AI2 source.
// ir_make_term_from_type_and_str: constructs an IR term from a type tag (Int) and string.
// TYPE GAP: takes [Int, Text] as a heterogeneous list — typed as Value in/out.
// ir_build_arg_list: builds a 1 or 2 element list of IR terms based on count.
// TYPE GAP: takes [Int, Value, Value] as a heterogeneous list — typed as Value in/out.
// ─────────── lib/core: prompt / report builders ───────────

// build_llm_prompt: concatenates header + newline + unknowns_text into LLM prompt.
// format_sweep_report: formats one PROPOSED sweep report entry (6-field pipe-delimited line).
// ─────────── lib/core: classification ───────────

// hole_classify: returns true if type_sig contains arrow_token (i.e. is a function type).
// parse_walk_result: extracts the kind prefix (before first pipe) from a WalkResult line.
// ─────────── lib/core: frontend ───────────

// shape_lookup: looks up the primary shape name for an artifact type.
// Delegates to bridge function frontend_lookup_shape.
// ─────────── lib/core: policy ───────────

// policy_kernel: range-check policy. Returns true if tid is in [0, 7].